the\nair pressure from the BME688. If the CO₂ reading drifts over the months (for example it never gets near \\~420 ppm\nwith the windows wide open), use the *Calibrate CO₂ sensor* maintenance\naction."},"24":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-22","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#air-quality-index-iaq","content":"**Air quality (IAQ)** is a number from 0 to 500 that Bosch's BSEC algorithm calculates from the BME688's gas\nreadings. It reacts to volatile compounds in the air: cooking, cleaning products, paint, perfume, people. Lower is\nbetter."},"25":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-23","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#air-quality-index-iaq","content":"The BME688 has no absolute scale: BSEC learns what clean and polluted air look like *in your room*, so the IAQ is\nrelative to the history of that room."},"26":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-24","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#air-quality-class","content":"**Air quality** turns the IAQ into words. The sensor's firmware uses these ranges:"},"27":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-25","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#air-quality-class","content":"Class"},"28":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-26","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#air-quality-class","content":"IAQ"},"29":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-27","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#air-quality-class","content":"**Excellent**"},"30":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-28","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#air-quality-class","content":"0–50"},"31":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-29","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#air-quality-class","content":"**Good**"},"32":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-30","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#air-quality-class","content":"51–100"},"33":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-31","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#air-quality-class","content":"**Lightly polluted**"},"34":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-32","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#air-quality-class","content":"101–150"},"35":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-33","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#air-quality-class","content":"**Moderately polluted**"},"36":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-34","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#air-quality-class","content":"151–200"},"37":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-35","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#air-quality-class","content":"**Heavily polluted**"},"38":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-36","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#air-quality-class","content":"201–250"},"39":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-37","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#air-quality-class","content":"**Severely polluted**"},"40":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-38","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#air-quality-class","content":"251–350"},"41":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-39","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#air-quality-class","content":"**Extremely polluted**"},"42":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-40","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#air-quality-class","content":"351 and up"},"43":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-41","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#air-quality-class","content":"The *Air quality changed* trigger and the *Air quality is … or worse*\ncondition use these classes."},"44":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-42","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#calibration","content":"**Air quality calibration** tells you how reliable the IAQ, the class and the VOC are right now. It does not\nmeasure anything itself."},"45":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-43","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#calibration","content":"State"},"46":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-44","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#calibration","content":"Meaning"},"47":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-45","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#calibration","content":"**Stabilizing**"},"48":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-46","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#calibration","content":"Just started; the gas sensor is still warming up. The values mean nothing yet."},"49":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-47","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#calibration","content":"**Uncertain**"},"50":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-48","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#calibration","content":"Too little history; the values are rough."},"51":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-49","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#calibration","content":"**Calibrating**"},"52":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-50","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#calibration","content":"BSEC is learning the room and getting better."},"53":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-51","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#calibration","content":"**Calibrated**"},"54":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-52","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#calibration","content":"BSEC knows the room. IAQ, class and VOC are reliable."},"55":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-53","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#calibration","content":"Getting to *Calibrated* takes hours to a few days. It goes fastest when the sensor experiences both fresh air\n(a window open) and polluted air. After a power cut or restart the state can drop back a step."},"56":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-54","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#calibration","content":"CO₂ comes from the separate SCD40 and does **not** depend on this calibration."},"57":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-55","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#voc","content":"**VOC** (ppm) is BSEC's estimate of the concentration of volatile organic compounds, derived from the same gas\nreadings as the IAQ. Use it as a trend (\"something is going on in the kitchen\") rather than as an absolute\nmeasurement."},"58":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-56","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#not-shown-on-the-device","content":"The sensor reports a few more air values that the app leaves off the tile on purpose:"},"59":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-57","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#not-shown-on-the-device","content":"Entity on the sensor"},"60":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-58","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#not-shown-on-the-device","content":"Why it is not shown"},"61":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-59","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#not-shown-on-the-device","content":"BME688 CO₂ equivalent"},"62":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-60","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#not-shown-on-the-device","content":"An estimate from the gas sensor; the real CO₂ from the SCD40 is shown instead."},"63":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-61","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#not-shown-on-the-device","content":"BME688 gas resistance"},"64":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-62","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#not-shown-on-the-device","content":"A raw value that BSEC already turns into IAQ and VOC."},"65":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-63","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#not-shown-on-the-device","content":"SCD40 temperature and humidity"},"66":{"id":"/docs/air-quality-64","page_id":"/docs/air-quality","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/air-quality#not-shown-on-the-device","content":"Duplicates of the BME688 values; the SCD40 uses them internally for its CO₂ reading."},"67":{"id":"/docs/changelog","page_id":"/docs/changelog","type":"page","content":"Changelog","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Documentation","Help"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/changelog"},"68":{"id":"/docs/changelog-0","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog","content":"All notable changes to the app."},"69":{"id":"/docs/changelog-1","page_id":"/docs/changelog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/changelog#unreleased","content":"\\[Unreleased]"},"70":{"id":"/docs/changelog-2","page_id":"/docs/changelog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/changelog#changed","content":"Changed"},"71":{"id":"/docs/changelog-3","page_id":"/docs/changelog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Added"},"72":{"id":"/docs/changelog-4","page_id":"/docs/changelog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/changelog#100---unreleased","content":"\\[1.0.0] - unreleased"},"73":{"id":"/docs/changelog-5","page_id":"/docs/changelog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/changelog#added-1","content":"Added"},"74":{"id":"/docs/changelog-6","page_id":"/docs/changelog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/changelog#changed-1","content":"Changed"},"75":{"id":"/docs/changelog-7","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog","content":"All notable changes to this app are documented here. The format follows\nKeep a Changelog and the app uses\nSemantic Versioning."},"76":{"id":"/docs/changelog-8","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#changed","content":"The app is now a Homey Python app on top of `homey-esphomedriver` (and `aioesphomeapi`) instead of\n`@2colors/esphome-native-api`. The library takes over the connection, reconnects, pairing (mDNS and *Add by IP…*)\nand the standard capabilities; sensors with an API encryption key can now be added."},"77":{"id":"/docs/changelog-9","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#changed","content":"Presence is `alarm_presence` and movement is `alarm_motion` (was `alarm_motion` and `sensy_moving`).\nExisting sensors must be removed and added again."},"78":{"id":"/docs/changelog-10","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#changed","content":"Requires Homey 13.0 or newer."},"79":{"id":"/docs/changelog-11","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#changed","content":"App id is `io.github.starredev.sensy`, so later Sensy-One products can be added as drivers of the same app.\nThe Node.js version (`io.github.starredev.sensys1pro`) is kept on the `node` branch and tag `node-1.0.0`."},"80":{"id":"/docs/changelog-12","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Diagnostic and configuration entities can be shown as capabilities from the device settings."},"81":{"id":"/docs/changelog-13","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"*Refresh capabilities* maintenance action."},"82":{"id":"/docs/changelog-14","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Air quality class (*Excellent* … *Extremely polluted*), its calibration state and VOC as capabilities, with an\n*Air quality changed* trigger and an *Air quality is X or worse* condition."},"83":{"id":"/docs/changelog-15","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Tracking settings of the radar: holding people who stand still (the firmware's holding engine, off by default),\nstationary speed, hold after standing still, hold time and jump distance; light and UV offsets."},"84":{"id":"/docs/changelog-16","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Settings for mirrored mounting, real-time environment readings and the buzzer's pitch and volume."},"85":{"id":"/docs/changelog-17","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Maintenance actions: calibrate the CO₂ sensor, restart the sensor, restart the radar."},"86":{"id":"/docs/changelog-18","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"The radar widget shows whether a person is moving, standing still or held."},"87":{"id":"/docs/changelog-19","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"A device warning and a *New firmware is available* trigger when Sensy-One releases a newer firmware."},"88":{"id":"/docs/changelog-20","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added","content":"Zone capabilities follow the zones drawn in the zone editor automatically."},"89":{"id":"/docs/changelog-21","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added-1","content":"S1 Pro Multi Sense device, discovered through mDNS and followed when its IP address changes."},"90":{"id":"/docs/changelog-22","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added-1","content":"Presence, movement and people count; temperature, humidity, pressure, IAQ, CO₂, light and UV."},"91":{"id":"/docs/changelog-23","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added-1","content":"Up to three zones with presence, movement and people sub-capabilities, shown only for zones that have an outline."},"92":{"id":"/docs/changelog-24","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added-1","content":"Flow cards: seven triggers, four conditions and two actions."},"93":{"id":"/docs/changelog-25","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added-1","content":"Device settings that stay in sync with the sensor in both directions."},"94":{"id":"/docs/changelog-26","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added-1","content":"Zone editor on the app settings page and the *Sensy radar* dashboard widget."},"95":{"id":"/docs/changelog-27","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added-1","content":"Works with the official Sensy-One firmware as well as the Homey edition; live target positions are read from whichever the sensor provides."},"96":{"id":"/docs/changelog-28","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added-1","content":"Adding a sensor by IP address or host name when mDNS discovery finds nothing."},"97":{"id":"/docs/changelog-29","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#added-1","content":"A device warning when the sensor's BLE proxy is switched on, since it makes the WiFi connection unstable and Homey does not use it."},"98":{"id":"/docs/changelog-30","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#changed-1","content":"App id is `io.github.starredev.sensys1pro` (was `nl.bryan.sensys1pro` during development)."},"99":{"id":"/docs/changelog-31","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#changed-1","content":"Rewritten as layered, test-covered ES modules; see CONTRIBUTING.md."},"100":{"id":"/docs/device","page_id":"/docs/device","type":"page","content":"The device","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Documentation","Using the app"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/device"},"101":{"id":"/docs/device-0","page_id":"/docs/device","tags":[],"type":"te