text","url":"/docs/settings","content":"Change a setting in Homey and the app writes it to the sensor right away."},"1646":{"id":"/docs/settings-11","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings","content":"Change it somewhere else (the sensor's web page, Home Assistant, another app) and the Homey setting follows\nabout a second later."},"1647":{"id":"/docs/settings-12","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings","content":"If the sensor is offline when you save, Homey shows *The sensor is not connected* and nothing is changed."},"1648":{"id":"/docs/settings-13","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings","content":"The exact ranges and defaults of every setting are in the settings reference."},"1649":{"id":"/docs/settings-14","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#detection","content":"Setting"},"1650":{"id":"/docs/settings-15","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#detection","content":"What it does"},"1651":{"id":"/docs/settings-16","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#detection","content":"**Detection range** (0–1800 cm)"},"1652":{"id":"/docs/settings-17","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#detection","content":"How far the radar looks. People further away are ignored. Also sets the size of the radar map in the zone editor and the widget."},"1653":{"id":"/docs/settings-18","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#detection","content":"**Presence hold time** (0–3600 s)"},"1654":{"id":"/docs/settings-19","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#detection","content":"How long *Presence* stays on after the radar last detected someone. Raise it if presence drops while people sit still for a long time."},"1655":{"id":"/docs/settings-20","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#detection","content":"**Movement threshold** (0–5000 cm/s)"},"1656":{"id":"/docs/settings-21","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#detection","content":"The minimum speed that counts as *Motion*. Raise it if small movements (breathing, typing) should not count."},"1657":{"id":"/docs/settings-22","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#detection","content":"**Track a single person**"},"1658":{"id":"/docs/settings-23","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#detection","content":"The radar reports at most one target. Useful in rooms where one person is expected and reflections cause ghost targets. With two people in the room it still reports only one."},"1659":{"id":"/docs/settings-24","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#detection","content":"**Mirrored mounting**"},"1660":{"id":"/docs/settings-25","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#detection","content":"Swaps left and right, for a sensor that is mounted upside down or faces the other way. Zones and the radar map follow."},"1661":{"id":"/docs/settings-26","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#detection","content":"**Real-time environment readings**"},"1662":{"id":"/docs/settings-27","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#detection","content":"On: temperature, humidity, CO₂ and the other climate values are sent as soon as they change. Off: once a minute, which means less traffic."},"1663":{"id":"/docs/settings-28","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#zone-1-zone-2-zone-3","content":"Each detection zone has its own:"},"1664":{"id":"/docs/settings-29","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#zone-1-zone-2-zone-3","content":"Setting"},"1665":{"id":"/docs/settings-30","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#zone-1-zone-2-zone-3","content":"What it does"},"1666":{"id":"/docs/settings-31","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#zone-1-zone-2-zone-3","content":"**Presence hold time** (0–3600 s)"},"1667":{"id":"/docs/settings-32","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#zone-1-zone-2-zone-3","content":"How long the zone's presence stays on after the last detection inside it."},"1668":{"id":"/docs/settings-33","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#zone-1-zone-2-zone-3","content":"**Movement threshold** (0–5000 cm/s)"},"1669":{"id":"/docs/settings-34","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#zone-1-zone-2-zone-3","content":"The minimum speed that counts as movement inside the zone."},"1670":{"id":"/docs/settings-35","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#zone-1-zone-2-zone-3","content":"These are the same values you can set in the zone editor and with the\n*Set zone presence hold time* flow card."},"1671":{"id":"/docs/settings-36","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#tracking","content":"The official firmware has a *holding engine*: it can keep a person in place when the radar briefly loses them,\nfor example someone who sits very still on a sofa. These settings tune how people are tracked."},"1672":{"id":"/docs/settings-37","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#tracking","content":"Setting"},"1673":{"id":"/docs/settings-38","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#tracking","content":"What it does"},"1674":{"id":"/docs/settings-39","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#tracking","content":"**Hold people who stand still**"},"1675":{"id":"/docs/settings-40","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#tracking","content":"Turns the holding engine on. **Off by default.** The two hold settings below only work when this is on."},"1676":{"id":"/docs/settings-41","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#tracking","content":"**Stationary speed** (0–100 cm/s)"},"1677":{"id":"/docs/settings-42","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#tracking","content":"Below this speed a person counts as standing still."},"1678":{"id":"/docs/settings-43","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#tracking","content":"**Hold after standing still** (0–120 s)"},"1679":{"id":"/docs/settings-44","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#tracking","content":"A person who stood still this long is *held*: their position stays even when the radar briefly loses them."},"1680":{"id":"/docs/settings-45","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#tracking","content":"**Hold time** (0–60 min)"},"1681":{"id":"/docs/settings-46","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#tracking","content":"How long a held person stays when the radar no longer sees them. People who disappear at the edge of the detection area are not held."},"1682":{"id":"/docs/settings-47","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#tracking","content":"**Jump distance** (5–300 cm)"},"1683":{"id":"/docs/settings-48","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#tracking","content":"A new measurement further than this from a person's last position counts as a new person. Lower values reduce ghost targets; too low and a quickly walking person is split in two."},"1684":{"id":"/docs/settings-49","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#tracking","content":"Turn on **Hold people who stand still**, keep **Hold after standing still** at about a minute and set\n**Hold time** to 15–30 minutes. Someone who watches a film without moving then stays present."},"1685":{"id":"/docs/settings-50","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#tracking","content":"People who walk out through the edge of the detection area are released straight away. If the door is in\nthe middle of what the radar sees, a person who sat still before leaving can be held until the hold time\nruns out; keep the hold time short in that case."},"1686":{"id":"/docs/settings-51","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#tracking","content":"The radar widget shows which people are moving, standing still or held."},"1687":{"id":"/docs/settings-52","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#calibration","content":"Setting"},"1688":{"id":"/docs/settings-53","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#calibration","content":"What it does"},"1689":{"id":"/docs/settings-54","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#calibration","content":"**Temperature offset** (−50 to 50 °C)"},"1690":{"id":"/docs/settings-55","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#calibration","content":"Added to the BME688 temperature. The sensor warms up a little from its own electronics; compare with a reference thermometer and correct here."},"1691":{"id":"/docs/settings-56","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#calibration","content":"**CO₂ sensor temperature offset** (−50 to 50 °C)"},"1692":{"id":"/docs/settings-57","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#calibration","content":"Temperature offset of the SCD40, which uses its temperature to compensate the CO₂ reading."},"1693":{"id":"/docs/settings-58","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#calibration","content":"**Light offset** (−10000 to 10000 lx)"},"1694":{"id":"/docs/settings-59","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#calibration","content":"Added to the light reading."},"1695":{"id":"/docs/settings-60","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#calibration","content":"**UV index offset** (−50 to 50)"},"1696":{"id":"/docs/settings-61","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#calibration","content":"Added to the UV index."},"1697":{"id":"/docs/settings-62","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#calibration","content":"To calibrate the CO₂ reading itself, use the *Calibrate CO₂ sensor*\nmaintenance action."},"1698":{"id":"/docs/settings-63","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#buzzer","content":"Setting"},"1699":{"id":"/docs/settings-64","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#buzzer","content":"What it does"},"1700":{"id":"/docs/settings-65","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#buzzer","content":"**Pitch** (100–8000 Hz)"},"1701":{"id":"/docs/settings-66","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#buzzer","content":"Pitch of the buzzer, for example for the *Beep* flow card."},"1702":{"id":"/docs/settings-67","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#buzzer","content":"**Volume** (0–100 %)"},"1703":{"id":"/docs/settings-68","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#buzzer","content":"Loudness of the buzzer."},"1704":{"id":"/docs/settings-69","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#device","content":"Setting"},"1705":{"id":"/docs/settings-70","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#device","content":"What it does"},"1706":{"id":"/docs/settings-71","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#device","content":"**Device class**"},"1707":{"id":"/docs/settings-72","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#device","content":"The kind of device Homey treats it as. *Auto* keeps *Sensor*; there is normally no reason to change it."},"1708":{"id":"/docs/settings-73","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#capabilities","content":"Setting"},"1709":{"id":"/docs/settings-74","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#capabilities","content":"What it does"},"1710":{"id":"/docs/settings-75","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#capabilities","content":"**Show diagnostic capabilities**"},"1711":{"id":"/docs/settings-76","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#capabilities","content":"Adds diagnostic values to the tile: WiFi network, signal strength, IP address, the ESP32's temperature and its connection status."},"1712":{"id":"/docs/settings-77","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#capabilities","content":"**Show configuration capabilities**"},"1713":{"id":"/docs/settings-78","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#capabilities","content":"Adds the sensor's remaining configuration entities as controls, such as the RGB LED, the radar's Bluetooth, the buzzer switch and the BLE proxy switch."},"1714":{"id":"/docs/settings-79","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#capabilities","content":"Turning these off removes the extra values again. See\nMaintenance and firmware for the full list."},"1715":{"id":"/docs/settings-80","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#device-information","content":"Read-only details that come from the sensor and the connection: IP address and port, whether an encryption key\nis used, manufacturer, model, MAC address, host name, ESPHome version, compilation time, project name and\nversion, Bluetooth MAC, the address of the sensor's web page and whether deep sleep is used."},"1716":{"id":"/docs/settings-81","page_id":"/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/settings#device-information","content":"The **Project** line shows the firmware version, for example `Sensy-One.S1 Pro Multi Sense v1.2.21`."},"1717":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","type":"page","content":"Troubleshooting and FAQ","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Documentation","Help"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/troubleshooting"},"1718":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-0","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Fixes for common problems, and short answers to common questions."},"1719":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-1","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/troubleshooting#the-sensor-is-not-found-when-adding-it","content":"The sensor is not found when adding it"},"1720":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-2","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/troubleshooting#the-device-keeps-going-offline","content":"The device keeps going offline"},"1721":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-3","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/troubleshooting#ghost-targets","content":"Ghost targets"},"1722":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-4","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/troubleshooting#presence-turns-off-while-someone-sits-still","content":"Presence turns off while someone sits still"},"1723":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-5","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/troubleshooting#presence-stays-on-in-an-empty-room","content":"Presence stays on in an empty room"},"1724":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-6","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/troubleshooting#zone-capabilities-are-missing","content":"Zone capabilities are missing"},"1725":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-7","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/troubleshooting#settings-do-not-stick","content":"Settings do not stick"},"1726":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-8","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/troubleshooting#co-readings-look-wrong","content":"CO₂ readings look wrong"},"1727":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-9","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/troubleshooting#air-quality-stays-good-while-it-smells","content":"Air quality stays \"Good\" while it smells"},"1728":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-10","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/troubleshooting#faq","content":"FAQ"},"1729":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-11","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/troubleshooting#getting-help","content":"Getting help"},"1730":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-12","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#the-sensor-is-not-found-when-adding-it","content":"Automatic discovery uses mDNS (`_esphomelib._tcp`), which does not cross networks, VLANs or some mesh WiFi\nsystems."},"1731":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-13","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#the-sensor-is-not-found-when-adding-it","content":"Choose **Add by IP…** in the list and enter the sensor's address (see\nAdding by IP address)."},"1732":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-14","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#the-sensor-is-not-found-when-adding-it","content":"Give the sensor a fixed IP address with a DHCP reservation in your router."},"1733":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-15","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#the-sensor-is-not-found-when-adding-it","content":"Make sure Homey can reach the sensor on TCP port 6053 (firewall rules between VLANs)."},"1734":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-16","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#the-sensor-is-not-found-when-adding-it","content":"Check that the sensor runs the official firmware: other ESPHome devices are not listed."},"1735":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-17","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#the-device-keeps-going-offline","content":"**Is the Bluetooth proxy on?** The device shows a warning when it is. Turn off **BLE | Proxy** on the\nsensor's web page. On the ESP32-C3, Bluetooth and WiFi share one radio, and with the proxy on the connection\ndrops every few minutes."},"1736":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-18","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#the-device-keeps-going-offline","content":"**WiFi signal.** Turn on *Show diagnostic capabilities* and look at\n*WiFi strength*. *Weak* or *Very weak* means the sensor needs a better spot or an access point closer by."},"1737":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-19","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#the-device-keeps-going-offline","content":"**Power.** Use a decent USB power supply; a weak supply makes the ESP32 restart under load."},"1738":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-20","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#the-device-keeps-going-offline","content":"**IP address changes.** Homey follows the sensor through mDNS. If mDNS does not work on your network, give\nthe sensor a fixed IP address and use Repair."},"1739":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-21","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#ghost-targets","content":"*The radar sees two people while I am alone*, or a second person that moves along with you."},"1740":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-22","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#ghost-targets","content":"The app shows exactly what the radar reports. Two common causes:"},"1741":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-23","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#ghost-targets","content":"**A real second target.** Pets are moving targets too. A cat walking through or lying on a chair shows up as a\nperson."},"1742":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-24","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#ghost-targets","content":"**Reflections (multipath).** Radar signals bounce off hard, flat surfaces such as mirrors, glass, tiles and\nmetal. The radar then sees you twice: once where you are, and once as a \"mirror image\" that moves along with\nyou, often in the opposite direction. Bathrooms are the classic case."},"1743":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-25","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#ghost-targets","content":"What helps, in this order:"},"1744":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-26","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#ghost-targets","content":"**Track a single person** in rooms where one person is expected, such as a bathroom.\nThe mirror image disappears."},"1745":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-27","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#ghost-targets","content":"**Point the sensor differently**, so it does not look straight at a mirror or glass wall."},"1746":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-28","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#ghost-targets","content":"**Lower the jump distance** (for example to 60 cm), so a reflection that appears\nsomewhere else is less likely to be taken for the same person."},"1747":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-29","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#ghost-targets","content":"**An exclusion zone** helps when the ghost always appears in the same place\n(a mirror, a window). It does not help against a ghost that moves along with you."},"1748":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-30","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#presence-turns-off-while-someone-sits-still","content":"Raise the **presence hold time**, for the room and for the zone in question."},"1749":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-31","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#presence-turns-off-while-someone-sits-still","content":"Turn on **Hold people who stand still** and set a longer **hold time**."},"1750":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-32","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#presence-turns-off-while-someone-sits-still","content":"Check that the person is within the detection range and not in the exclusion zone."},"1751":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-33","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#presence-stays-on-in-an-empty-room","content":"Look at the zone editor or the widget: is there a marker where nobody is? Then\nsomething moves there (a fan, curtains, a plant near a heater) or a reflection shows up: cover it with an\nexclusion zone."},"1752":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-34","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#presence-stays-on-in-an-empty-room","content":"A faded, dashed marker is a **held** person. Lower the hold time, or turn the holding\nengine off."},"1753":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-35","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#presence-stays-on-in-an-empty-room","content":"Lower the presence hold time if it is very long."},"1754":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-36","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#zone-capabilities-are-missing","content":"They appear a few seconds after you save a zone with **at least three points** in the zone editor. If the\nsensor was offline at that moment, they appear when it reconnects. *Refresh capabilities* keeps them."},"1755":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-37","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#settings-do-not-stick","content":"If a setting jumps back after you saved it, the sensor was probably offline: Homey then shows *The sensor is not\nconnected* and changes nothing. Settings changed on the sensor's own web page show up in Homey after about a\nsecond; that is the sync working, not an error."},"1756":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-38","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#co-readings-look-wrong","content":"Right after a restart the SCD40 needs a few minutes to settle."},"1757":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-39","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#co-readings-look-wrong","content":"If readings have drifted, calibrate the CO₂ sensor, outdoors."},"1758":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-40","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#air-quality-stays-good-while-it-smells","content":"The IAQ, the class and VOC are only reliable once the calibration shows\n*Calibrated*, which can take a few days. CO₂ (from the SCD40) is reliable from the start."},"1759":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-41","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#faq","content":"No. Homey talks to the sensor on your local network. The only outbound request is a version check against\nSensy-One's GitHub releases page every six hours, for the firmware notice."},"1760":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-42","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#faq","content":"No. The app uses the ESPHome native API directly."},"1761":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-43","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#faq","content":"Yes. The native API accepts several clients at once. Settings and zones changed in Home Assistant show up in\nHomey (and the other way round)."},"1762":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-44","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#faq","content":"Up to three at a time; that is the limit of the radar."},"1763":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-45","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#faq","content":"Yes. That is what mmWave radar is good at. Tune the hold times and the tracking for\nrooms where people stay still for a long time, such as a living room or bedroom."},"1764":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-46","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#faq","content":"Radar passes through thin, non-metallic materials such as drywall or a wooden door to some extent. Limit the\ndetection range and use an exclusion zone if it picks\nup movement in the next room."},"1765":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-47","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#faq","content":"Not reliably; a cat or dog is a moving target too, and the radar only sees positions on the floor plan, not\nheight. Zones and the people count often help, for example by only reacting to the sofa zone."},"1766":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-48","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#faq","content":"On the sensor itself. They survive a Homey restart, an app reinstall and re-adding the device."},"1767":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-49","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#faq","content":"*Presence* means someone is there (also when still); *Motion* means someone moves. Use *Presence* for lights\nand heating, *Motion* for things that should react to activity."},"1768":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-50","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#faq","content":"No; it tells you when there is an update. Install it from the sensor's web page."},"1769":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-51","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#faq","content":"The firmware only uses it during first-time setup. You can control it from Homey after turning on\n*Show configuration capabilities*."},"1770":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-52","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#faq","content":"See Coming from the previous version."},"1771":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-53","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#faq","content":"No. It is an unofficial community project, open source under the MIT licence."},"1772":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-54","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#getting-help","content":"Open an issue on GitHub and include:"},"1773":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-55","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#getting-help","content":"the app version (Settings → Apps → Sensy S1 Pro) and your Homey model and firmware;"},"1774":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-56","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#getting-help","content":"the sensor firmware (the device setting *Project*);"},"1775":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-57","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#getting-help","content":"what you expected and what happened."},"1776":{"id":"/docs/troubleshooting-58","page_id":"/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/troubleshooting#getting-help","content":"A diagnostics report helps a lot: **Settings → Apps → Sensy S1 Pro → Send diagnostics report**, then mention the\ncode it shows in the issue."},"1777":{"id":"/docs/widget","page_id":"/docs/widget","type":"page","content":"Radar widget","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Documentation","Using the app"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/widget"},"1778":{"id":"/docs/widget-0","page_id":"/docs/widget","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/widget","content":"A live top-down radar of the room on your Homey dashboard."},"1779":{"id":"/docs/widget-1","page_id":"/docs/widget","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/widget#adding-the-widget","content":"Adding the widget"},"1780":{"id":"/docs/widget-2","page_id":"/docs/widget","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/widget#what-you-see","content":"What you see"},"1781":{"id":"/docs/widget-3","page_id":"/docs/widget","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/widget#markers","content":"Markers"},"1782":{"id":"/docs/widget-4","page_id":"/docs/widget","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/widget#updates","content":"Updates"},"1783":{"id":"/docs/widget-5","page_id":"/docs/widget","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/widget","content":"The **Sensy radar** widget shows a live top-down radar of one sensor on a Homey dashboard: the people it sees,\nyour zones, and whether anyone is present."},"1784":{"id":"/docs/widget-6","page_id":"/docs/widget","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/widget#adding-the-widget","content":"Open a dashboard and choose **Edit**."},"1785":{"id":"/docs/widget-7","page_id":"/docs/widget","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/widget#adding-the-widget","content":"Add a widget and pick **Sensy radar** (from the Sensy S1 Pro app)."},"1786":{"id":"/docs/widget-8","page_id":"/docs/widget","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/widget#adding-the-widget","content":"In the widget settings, choose the **Sensor**. Start typing its name; the list also shows whether each sensor\nis online."},"1787":{"id":"/docs/widget-9","page_id":"/docs/widget","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/widget#adding-the-widget","content":"Without a chosen sensor, the widget shows the first S1 Pro of the app."},"1788":{"id":"/docs/widget-10","page_id":"/docs/widget","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/widget#what-you-see","content":"**Header**: a dot that is lit while the sensor is connected, the sensor's name, and a status pill:"},"1789":{"id":"/docs/widget-11","page_id":"/docs/widget","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/widget#what-you-see","content":"*Empty* when nobody is present;"},"1790":{"id":"/docs/widget-12","page_id":"/docs/widget","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/widget#what-you-see","content":"*2 present* when people are present but not moving;"},"1791":{"id":"/docs/widget-13","page_id":"/docs/widget","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/widget#what-you-see","content":"*2 moving* when someone moves."},"1792":{"id":"/docs/widget-14","page_id":"/docs/widget","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/widget#what-you-see","content":"**Radar map**: the sensor at the bottom centre, the field of view, distance lines, and your zones. A zone\nlights up while someone is inside it. The exclusion zone is drawn in red."},"1793":{"id":"/docs/widget-15","page_id":"/docs/widget","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/widget#what-you-see","content":"**People** as numbered markers that glide to their new position, with a short fading trail."},"1794":{"id":"/docs/widget-16","page_id":"/docs/widget","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/widget#what-you-see","content":"The map scales with the detection range: a larger range zooms out."},"1795":{"id":"/docs/widget-17","page_id":"/docs/widget","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/widget#markers","content":"Marker"},"1796":{"id":"/docs/widget-18","page_id":"/docs/widget","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/widget#markers","content":"Meaning"},"1797":{"id":"/docs/widget-19","page_id":"/docs/widget","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/widget#markers","content":"**Solid**"},"1798":{"id":"/docs/widget-20","page_id":"/docs/widget","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/widget#markers","content":"The person moves."},"1799":{"id":"/docs/widget-21","page_id":"/docs/widget","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/widget#markers","content":"**Dashed ring**"},"1800":{"id":"/docs/widget-22","page_id":"/docs/widget","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/widget#markers","content":"The person stands or sits still (below the *Stationary speed*)."},"1801":{"id":"/docs/widget-23","page_id":"/docs/widget","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/widget#markers","content":"**Dashed and faded**"},"1802":{"id":"/docs/widget-24","page_id":"/docs/widget","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/widget#markers","content":"The person stood still long enough to be *held*: the holding engine keeps them in place, also when the radar briefly loses them."},"1803":{"id":"/docs/widget-25","page_id":"/docs/widget","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/widget#markers","content":"**Trail**"},"1804":{"id":"/docs/widget-26","page_id":"/docs/widget","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/widget#markers","content":"The last positions, fading out."},"1805":{"id":"/docs/widget-27","page_id":"/docs/widget","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/widget#markers","content":"Each of the three people the radar can track has its own colour (blue, orange, green), so you can follow one\nperson across the map. The same markers appear in the zone editor."},"1806":{"id":"/docs/widget-28","page_id":"/docs/widget","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/widget#markers","content":"Firmware without per-person states (for example a custom build) shows every marker as solid."},"1807":{"id":"/docs/widget-29","page_id":"/docs/widget","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/widget#updates","content":"The widget updates live, several times per second while people move, without polling. When the sensor goes\noffline the dot turns off, and it picks up again by itself when the sensor is back. Changes to zones (from the\nzone editor or elsewhere) appear right away."},"1808":{"id":"/docs/zones","page_id":"/docs/zones","type":"page","content":"Zones","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Documentation","Using the app"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/zones"},"1809":{"id":"/docs/zones-0","page_id":"/docs/zones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/zones","content":"Draw up to three zones and an exclusion zone on a live radar map."},"1810":{"id":"/docs/zones-1","page_id":"/docs/zones","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/zones#opening-the-zone-editor","content":"Opening the zone editor"},"1811":{"id":"/docs/zones-2","page_id":"/docs/zones","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/zones#drawing-a-zone","content":"Drawing a zone"},"1812":{"id":"/docs/zones-3","page_id":"/docs/zones","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/zones#zone-settings","content":"Zone settings"},"1813":{"id":"/docs/zones-4","page_id":"/docs/zones","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/zones#the-exclusion-zone","content":"The exclusion zone"},"1814":{"id":"/docs/zones-5","page_id":"/docs/zones","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/zones#rules-and-limits","content":"Rules and limits"},"1815":{"id":"/docs/zones-6","page_id":"/docs/zones","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/zones#zones-from-elsewhere","content":"Zones from elsewhere"},"1816":{"id":"/docs/zones-7","page_id":"/docs/zones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/zones","content":"Zones split a room into areas: the sofa, the desk, the bed, the bath. Each zone reports its own presence,\nmovement and people count, has its own flow cards and its own settings. The S1 Pro stores up to\n**three detection zones** and one **exclusion zone** in the sensor itself, so they keep working when Homey\nrestarts."},"1817":{"id":"/docs/zones-8","page_id":"/docs/zones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/zones#opening-the-zone-editor","content":"**Settings → Apps → Sensy S1 Pro → Configure** (or *App settings* in the Homey web app)."},"1818":{"id":"/docs/zones-9","page_id":"/docs/zones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/zones#opening-the-zone-editor","content":"At the top you choose the zone: **1**, **2**, **3** or **Exclusion**. With more than one sensor, a list lets you\nchoose the sensor first."},"1819":{"id":"/docs/zones-10","page_id":"/docs/zones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/zones#opening-the-zone-editor","content":"The map is a top-down view of what the radar sees: the sensor sits at the bottom centre, the field of view fans\nout upwards, and grid lines mark the distance (every metre, or every two metres for a large detection range). People show up as numbered dots that move live while you walk\naround (see the radar widget markers). Next to the zone tabs, a live label says who is\nthere: *Nobody present*, *1 present* or *1 present · moving*."},"1820":{"id":"/docs/zones-11","page_id":"/docs/zones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/zones#drawing-a-zone","content":"Choose the zone tab."},"1821":{"id":"/docs/zones-12","page_id":"/docs/zones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/zones#drawing-a-zone","content":"**Tap the map** to place a corner point. Place **3 to 8** points; the outline closes by itself."},"1822":{"id":"/docs/zones-13","page_id":"/docs/zones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/zones#drawing-a-zone","content":"**Drag** a point to move it."},"1823":{"id":"/docs/zones-14","page_id":"/docs/zones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/zones#drawing-a-zone","content":"**Undo point** removes the last point; **Clear zone** removes all points."},"1824":{"id":"/docs/zones-15","page_id":"/docs/zones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/zones#drawing-a-zone","content":"**Save** writes the zone to the sensor."},"1825":{"id":"/docs/zones-16","page_id":"/docs/zones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/zones#drawing-a-zone","content":"The status line tells you where you are: *2 more point(s) needed*, *5 points · not saved*, *Zone saved to the\nsensor*. If you switch to another zone with unsaved changes, the editor asks first."},"1826":{"id":"/docs/zones-17","page_id":"/docs/zones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/zones#drawing-a-zone","content":"Stand in each corner of the area you want, look where your dot is on the map, and tap there. That is the\nmost reliable way to match zones to the real room."},"1827":{"id":"/docs/zones-18","page_id":"/docs/zones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/zones#drawing-a-zone","content":"After saving, the zone's capabilities (*Zone N presence*, *Zone N movement*, *People in zone N*) appear on the\ndevice within a few seconds. Clearing a zone and saving removes them again."},"1828":{"id":"/docs/zones-19","page_id":"/docs/zones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/zones#zone-settings","content":"Below the map, **Settings for this zone** has the zone's own:"},"1829":{"id":"/docs/zones-20","page_id":"/docs/zones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/zones#zone-settings","content":"Setting"},"1830":{"id":"/docs/zones-21","page_id":"/docs/zones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/zones#zone-settings","content":"What it does"},"1831":{"id":"/docs/zones-22","page_id":"/docs/zones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/zones#zone-settings","content":"**Presence hold time (s)**"},"1832":{"id":"/docs/zones-23","page_id":"/docs/zones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/zones#zone-settings","content":"How long the zone stays occupied after the last detection inside it (0–3600 s)."},"1833":{"id":"/docs/zones-24","page_id":"/docs/zones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/zones#zone-settings","content":"**Movement threshold (cm/s)**"},"1834":{"id":"/docs/zones-25","page_id":"/docs/zones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/zones#zone-settings","content":"The minimum speed that counts as movement inside the zone (0–5000 cm/s)."},"1835":{"id":"/docs/zones-26","page_id":"/docs/zones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/zones#zone-settings","content":"Choose **Save settings** to write them. The same values are in the device settings."},"1836":{"id":"/docs/zones-27","page_id":"/docs/zones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/zones#the-exclusion-zone","content":"The exclusion zone masks out an area: the firmware discards every radar measurement inside it, so whatever moves\nthere counts neither for the room nor for any zone. Use it for things that move but are not people:"},"1837":{"id":"/docs/zones-28","page_id":"/docs/zones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/zones#the-exclusion-zone","content":"a ceiling or desk fan;"},"1838":{"id":"/docs/zones-29","page_id":"/docs/zones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/zones#the-exclusion-zone","content":"curtains that move in a draught;"},"1839":{"id":"/docs/zones-30","page_id":"/docs/zones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/zones#the-exclusion-zone","content":"a door to a busy hallway;"},"1840":{"id":"/docs/zones-31","page_id":"/docs/zones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/zones#the-exclusion-zone","content":"a reflection that keeps showing up in the same place."},"1841":{"id":"/docs/zones-32","page_id":"/docs/zones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/zones#the-exclusion-zone","content":"It has no presence of its own and no settings. On the map it is drawn in red."},"1842":{"id":"/docs/zones-33","page_id":"/docs/zones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/zones#rules-and-limits","content":"A zone has **0 points** (off) or **3 to 8 points**."},"1843":{"id":"/docs/zones-34","page_id":"/docs/zones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/zones#rules-and-limits","content":"Coordinates are whole centimetres within ±1800 cm."},"1844":{"id":"/docs/zones-35","page_id":"/docs/zones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/zones#rules-and-limits","content":"Only people within the detection range count, so a zone (partly) beyond it never sees anyone there."},"1845":{"id":"/docs/zones-36","page_id":"/docs/zones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/zones#rules-and-limits","content":"Zones may overlap; a person can be in several zones at once."},"1846":{"id":"/docs/zones-37","page_id":"/docs/zones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/zones#rules-and-limits","content":"While saving, the app first turns the zone off and then rewrites its points, so the sensor never evaluates a\nhalf-saved outline."},"1847":{"id":"/docs/zones-38","page_id":"/docs/zones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/zones#rules-and-limits","content":"Flows only fire for zones that have an outline. Values of zones that are not drawn are ignored."},"1848":{"id":"/docs/zones-39","page_id":"/docs/zones","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/zones#zones-from-elsewhere","content":"Zones drawn on the sensor's own web page or by another app are the same zones: the editor shows them, and the\ndevice gets their capabilities as soon as they appear on the sensor."},"1849":{"id":"/docs/developers/architecture","page_id":"/docs/developers/architecture","type":"page","content":"Architecture","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Developers"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/developers/architecture"},"1850":{"id":"/docs/developers/architecture-0","page_id":"/docs/developers/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/architecture","content":"Layers, the main classes and how data flows."},"1851":{"id":"/docs/developers/architecture-1","page_id":"/docs/developers/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/developers/architecture#repository-layout","content":"Repository layout"},"1852":{"id":"/docs/developers/architecture-2","page_id":"/docs/developers/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/developers/architecture#layers","content":"Layers"},"1853":{"id":"/docs/developers/architecture-3","page_id":"/docs/developers/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/developers/architecture#main-classes","content":"Main classes"},"1854":{"id":"/docs/developers/architecture-4","page_id":"/docs/developers/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/developers/architecture#data-flow","content":"Data flow"},"1855":{"id":"/docs/developers/architecture-5","page_id":"/docs/developers/architecture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/developers/architecture#notable-design-decisions","content":"Notable design decisions"},"1856":{"id":"/docs/developers/architecture-6","page_id":"/docs/developers/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/architecture#repository-layout","content":"`app.json` is generated from `.homeycompose/` and `drivers/*/*.compose.json`; never edit it by hand."},"1857":{"id":"/docs/developers/architecture-7","page_id":"/docs/developers/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/architecture#layers","content":"Imports only point downwards:"},"1858":{"id":"/docs/developers/architecture-8","page_id":"/docs/developers/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/architecture#layers","content":"`lib/sensor` never imports `homey`, the ESPHome client or `homey-esphomedriver`. It talks to the sensor\nthrough the `EntityPort` protocol and reports through the `SensorObserver` protocol, so it runs under plain\npytest with fakes."},"1859":{"id":"/docs/developers/architecture-9","page_id":"/docs/developers/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/architecture#layers","content":"`lib/esphome` implements the `EntityPort` on top of the library's Native API session."},"1860":{"id":"/docs/developers/architecture-10","page_id":"/docs/developers/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/architecture#layers","content":"`lib/homey` adapts the model to Homey: capabilities, flows, settings, realtime events and the web API."},"1861":{"id":"/docs/developers/architecture-11","page_id":"/docs/developers/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/architecture#layers","content":"The entry points are thin. They wire the pieces together and contain no domain logic."},"1862":{"id":"/docs/developers/architecture-12","page_id":"/docs/developers/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/architecture#layers","content":"The Homey Python runtime loads the app as the package `app` (`app.app`, `app.drivers.s1pro.device`,\n`app.widgets.radar.api`), so `lib` is never a top-level module at runtime. All app code imports itself\nrelatively (`from ...lib.sensor.zone import Zone`). A test guards this."},"1863":{"id":"/docs/developers/architecture-13","page_id":"/docs/developers/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/architecture#main-classes","content":"Class"},"1864":{"id":"/docs/developers/architecture-14","page_id":"/docs/developers/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/architecture#main-classes","content":"Module"},"1865":{"id":"/docs/developers/architecture-15","page_id":"/docs/developers/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/architecture#main-classes","content":"Responsibility"},"1866":{"id":"/docs/developers/architecture-16","page_id":"/docs/developers/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/architecture#main-classes","content":"`S1ProProfile`"},"1867":{"id":"/docs/developers/architecture-17","page_id":"/docs/developers/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/architecture#main-classes","content":"`lib/sensor/profile.py`"},"1868":{"id":"/docs/developers/architecture-18","page_id":"/docs/developers/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/architecture#main-classes","content":"Everything firmware-specific: entity ids, which entities become capabilities, setting bindings, target feeds, limits."},"1869":{"id":"/docs/developers/architecture-19","page_id":"/docs/developers/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/architecture#main-classes","content":"`S1ProSensor`"},"1870":{"id":"/docs/developers/architecture-20","page_id":"/docs/developers/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/architecture#main-classes","content":"`lib/sensor/sensor.py`"},"1871":{"id":"/docs/developers/architecture-21","page_id":"/docs/developers/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/architecture#main-classes","content":"The model of one sensor: queries (presence, zones, targets, air