rl":"/docs/developers/architecture#main-classes","content":"`FirmwareCatalog`"},"1909":{"id":"/docs/developers/architecture-59","page_id":"/docs/developers/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/architecture#main-classes","content":"`lib/homey/firmware.py`"},"1910":{"id":"/docs/developers/architecture-60","page_id":"/docs/developers/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/architecture#main-classes","content":"Latest official release from GitHub, cached for six hours."},"1911":{"id":"/docs/developers/architecture-61","page_id":"/docs/developers/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/architecture#main-classes","content":"`DeviceWarnings`"},"1912":{"id":"/docs/developers/architecture-62","page_id":"/docs/developers/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/architecture#main-classes","content":"`lib/homey/warnings.py`"},"1913":{"id":"/docs/developers/architecture-63","page_id":"/docs/developers/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/architecture#main-classes","content":"Combines several warnings into Homey's single device warning."},"1914":{"id":"/docs/developers/architecture-64","page_id":"/docs/developers/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/architecture#data-flow","content":"Commands go the other way: a flow card, the web API or a settings change calls the model\n(`set_zone_outline`, `set_zone_options`, `apply_settings`, `beep`), which writes entities through the port.\nMaintenance buttons are pressed by the library itself."},"1915":{"id":"/docs/developers/architecture-65","page_id":"/docs/developers/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/architecture#notable-design-decisions","content":"**Capabilities are owned by the library.** All capabilities, including the per-zone ones, are mapped by\n`homey-esphomedriver`. The app only decides *which* through its brand profile. That keeps\n*Refresh capabilities* working without special cases. See homey-esphomedriver."},"1916":{"id":"/docs/developers/architecture-66","page_id":"/docs/developers/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/architecture#notable-design-decisions","content":"**Zones follow the drawn outlines.** Whether a zone exists is the *value* of `zone_N_points_count`, which the\nlibrary's pair-time mapping never sees. The device stores its drawn zones and returns a per-device brand profile\n(`SensyBrandProfile.with_zones`). When the outlines change, it presses the library's own refresh action."},"1917":{"id":"/docs/developers/architecture-67","page_id":"/docs/developers/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/architecture#notable-design-decisions","content":"**Settings live on the sensor.** The sensor is the source of truth. Homey settings mirror it both ways, debounced\nby a second, so settings changed in other tools show up in Homey."},"1918":{"id":"/docs/developers/architecture-68","page_id":"/docs/developers/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/architecture#notable-design-decisions","content":"**No flows from re-sent values.** After every (re)connect the `ValueTracker` forgets which values it has seen;\nthe first value of every entity is then *initial* and never fires a trigger."},"1919":{"id":"/docs/developers/architecture-69","page_id":"/docs/developers/architecture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/architecture#notable-design-decisions","content":"**Firmware differences live in the profile.** The official firmware reports target positions on every radar\nframe as `target_N_x`/`target_N_y` (with `(0, 0)` for an empty slot, completed by `y`); the older Homey edition\nsent `live_tN_x`/`live_tN_y` only on change, with `-9999` for empty. Each is a `TargetFeed` in the profile."},"1920":{"id":"/docs/developers/development","page_id":"/docs/developers/development","type":"page","content":"Development setup","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Developers"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/developers/development"},"1921":{"id":"/docs/developers/development-0","page_id":"/docs/developers/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/development","content":"Tools, running the app on your Homey, Windows notes."},"1922":{"id":"/docs/developers/development-1","page_id":"/docs/developers/development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/developers/development#tools","content":"Tools"},"1923":{"id":"/docs/developers/development-2","page_id":"/docs/developers/development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/developers/development#first-time","content":"First time"},"1924":{"id":"/docs/developers/development-3","page_id":"/docs/developers/development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/developers/development#running-on-your-homey","content":"Running on your Homey"},"1925":{"id":"/docs/developers/development-4","page_id":"/docs/developers/development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/developers/development#trying-code-against-a-real-sensor","content":"Trying code against a real sensor"},"1926":{"id":"/docs/developers/development-5","page_id":"/docs/developers/development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/developers/development#windows","content":"Windows"},"1927":{"id":"/docs/developers/development-6","page_id":"/docs/developers/development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/developers/development#code-style","content":"Code style"},"1928":{"id":"/docs/developers/development-7","page_id":"/docs/developers/development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/developers/development#adding-things","content":"Adding things"},"1929":{"id":"/docs/developers/development-8","page_id":"/docs/developers/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/development#tools","content":"**Python 3.14** and uv"},"1930":{"id":"/docs/developers/development-9","page_id":"/docs/developers/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/development#tools","content":"**Node.js 22** and the Homey CLI: `npm install --global homey`"},"1931":{"id":"/docs/developers/development-10","page_id":"/docs/developers/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/development#tools","content":"**Docker**: the Homey CLI compiles the Python dependencies for arm64 and amd64 in containers, and runs the app\nlocally with `homey app run`"},"1932":{"id":"/docs/developers/development-11","page_id":"/docs/developers/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/development#first-time","content":"`requirements-dev.txt` installs the runtime libraries (`aioesphomeapi`, `homey-esphomedriver`), the Homey SDK type\nstubs (`homey-stubs`) and the tools (pytest, pyright, ruff). The Homey SDK itself only exists inside the Homey\nruntime; tests never import it."},"1933":{"id":"/docs/developers/development-12","page_id":"/docs/developers/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/development#running-on-your-homey","content":"`homey app run` installs a development copy that is removed again when the session ends, even if you\ninstalled the same app id with `homey app install` in the meantime. Stop the run session first, then install."},"1934":{"id":"/docs/developers/development-13","page_id":"/docs/developers/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/development#running-on-your-homey","content":"With `homey app run` the app runs on your computer, so Homey has no CPU or memory figures for it. Install it\nto see those."},"1935":{"id":"/docs/developers/development-14","page_id":"/docs/developers/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/development#trying-code-against-a-real-sensor","content":"The domain model and the entity port can run outside Homey. A script like this connects the library's session to\nthe model, which is handy to check behaviour against a real sensor:"},"1936":{"id":"/docs/developers/development-15","page_id":"/docs/developers/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/development#windows","content":"The compiled dependency cache (`python_packages/*/.venv`) contains Linux symbolic links. Without Developer Mode,\nWindows cannot copy them, and the CLI fails with *Error while collecting cross-compiled virtual environment*\n(`EPERM … symlink`)."},"1937":{"id":"/docs/developers/development-16","page_id":"/docs/developers/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/development#windows","content":"Either enable **Developer Mode** in Windows, or delete the links once after the dependencies were compiled; the CLI\nremoves them from the build anyway:"},"1938":{"id":"/docs/developers/development-17","page_id":"/docs/developers/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/development#windows","content":"Build the dependencies from PowerShell or a terminal where Docker is on the `PATH`."},"1939":{"id":"/docs/developers/development-18","page_id":"/docs/developers/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/development#code-style","content":"Ruff and Pyright enforce the style; `ruff check --fix . && ruff format .` fixes most of it."},"1940":{"id":"/docs/developers/development-19","page_id":"/docs/developers/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/development#code-style","content":"Classes with type hints and docstrings; collaborators are injected, protocols describe the ports."},"1941":{"id":"/docs/developers/development-20","page_id":"/docs/developers/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/development#code-style","content":"Readability over brevity: one statement per line, no one-line `if x: return`, written-out loops where a dense\ncomprehension would hide the intent, blank lines before `return`."},"1942":{"id":"/docs/developers/development-21","page_id":"/docs/developers/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/development#code-style","content":"New behaviour comes with tests."},"1943":{"id":"/docs/developers/development-22","page_id":"/docs/developers/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/development#code-style","content":"The browser code follows the ESLint rules in `eslint.config.js` (`npm run lint:fix`)."},"1944":{"id":"/docs/developers/development-23","page_id":"/docs/developers/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/development#adding-things","content":"**A sensor reading**: add the entity to `S1ProProfile.CAPABILITIES`, with `None` to keep the capability the\nlibrary picks or a capability id to remap it. For a custom capability, add it under `.homeycompose/capabilities/`\nand to the `capabilities` list in `drivers/s1pro/driver.compose.json`. Raise `SensyBrandProfile.VERSION` so\nexisting devices refresh."},"1945":{"id":"/docs/developers/development-24","page_id":"/docs/developers/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/development#adding-things","content":"**A setting**: add a binding to `S1ProProfile.SETTINGS` and the setting to\n`drivers/s1pro/driver.settings.compose.json` with the same id."},"1946":{"id":"/docs/developers/development-25","page_id":"/docs/developers/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/development#adding-things","content":"**A flow trigger**: declare it in `drivers/s1pro/driver.flow.compose.json`, add (or reuse) a domain event in\n`lib/sensor/events.py` that `S1ProSensor` raises, map it in `FlowCards.translate` and add the id to `Cards`."},"1947":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","type":"page","content":"homey-esphomedriver","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Developers"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver"},"1948":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-0","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","content":"What the shared ESPHome library does and how this app builds on it."},"1949":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-1","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#what-the-library-does","content":"What the library does"},"1950":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-2","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#what-this-app-adds","content":"What this app adds"},"1951":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-3","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#hooks-used","content":"Hooks used"},"1952":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-4","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#refresh-rules","content":"Refresh rules"},"1953":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-5","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#upgrading-the-library","content":"Upgrading the library"},"1954":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-6","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","content":"`homey-esphomedriver` by Abe Haverkamp is the shared ESPHome\nlayer for Homey Python apps. The generic ESPHome app uses it\nfor any ESPHome node; brand apps like this one use the same core for their own products."},"1955":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-7","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#what-the-library-does","content":"**Discovery and pairing**: mDNS discovery, *Add by IP…*, encryption keys, repair."},"1956":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-8","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#what-the-library-does","content":"**The Native API session**: connect, reconnect with back-off, follow IP changes, availability."},"1957":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-9","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#what-the-library-does","content":"**Entity mapping**: turns ESPHome entities into Homey capabilities (sensors, binary sensors, switches, lights,\nbuttons, numbers, text sensors and many more), writes their values and handles commands."},"1958":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-10","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#what-the-library-does","content":"**Defaults**: compose templates (`esphome-defaults`), pair and repair views, generic flow cards, locales and\ncapability icons, synced into the app with `esphome-homey sync`."},"1959":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-11","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#what-this-app-adds","content":"Need"},"1960":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-12","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#what-this-app-adds","content":"How"},"1961":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-13","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#what-this-app-adds","content":"Only show the S1 Pro's primary entities"},"1962":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-14","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#what-this-app-adds","content":"`SensyBrandProfile.skip_entity` whitelists entities without a category through `S1ProProfile.CAPABILITIES`. Diagnostic and configuration entities keep the library behaviour (hidden until the user turns them on)."},"1963":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-15","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#what-this-app-adds","content":"Better capabilities for some entities"},"1964":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-16","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#what-this-app-adds","content":"`device_entities` remaps `all_targets_count` → `sensy_people`, `bme688_iaq` → `sensy_iaq`, and the air quality texts to enum capabilities."},"1965":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-17","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#what-this-app-adds","content":"Zone capabilities only for drawn zones"},"1966":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-18","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#what-this-app-adds","content":"`S1ProDevice.brand_profile` returns `SensyBrandProfile.with_zones(drawn)`; zone entities of drawn zones are mapped to `sensy_zone_*.zoneN` with localised titles."},"1967":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-19","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#what-this-app-adds","content":"Maintenance actions"},"1968":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-20","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#what-this-app-adds","content":"`after_map` adds `button.calibrate_co2`, `button.restart` and `button.restart_radar` with the button entity's key; the library presses `button.*` capabilities that carry a key."},"1969":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-21","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#what-this-app-adds","content":"One device class"},"1970":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-22","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#what-this-app-adds","content":"`device_class_for` always returns `sensor`, also when LED or switches are shown."},"1971":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-23","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#what-this-app-adds","content":"Everything beyond capabilities"},"1972":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-24","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#what-this-app-adds","content":"`EsphomeEntities` opens a second state subscription on the library's session (`client.api.subscribe_states`) and feeds the domain model."},"1973":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-25","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#what-this-app-adds","content":"Disconnects"},"1974":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-26","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#what-this-app-adds","content":"`aioesphomeapi`'s public `APIClient.add_connection_closed_callback`."},"1975":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-27","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#hooks-used","content":"Only documented hooks and public API:"},"1976":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-28","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#hooks-used","content":"`EspHomeDriver.on_esphome_init` registers the app's flow cards."},"1977":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-29","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#hooks-used","content":"`EspHomeDevice.on_esphome_init`, `on_esphome_connected` and `on_esphome_uninit` wire the domain model."},"1978":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-30","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#hooks-used","content":"`EspHomeDevice.brand_profile` (a public property) is overridden per device."},"1979":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-31","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#hooks-used","content":"`Device.trigger_capability_listener(\"button.refresh\", True)` presses the library's refresh action."},"1980":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-32","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#refresh-rules","content":"The device triggers a refresh itself when:"},"1981":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-33","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#refresh-rules","content":"the drawn zones differ from the zone capabilities it has;"},"1982":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-34","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#refresh-rules","content":"the brand profile's `VERSION` is newer than the one the device was last mapped with (stored as\n`profile_version`), so app updates that add capabilities reach existing devices;"},"1983":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-35","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#refresh-rules","content":"zone capabilities are inconsistent (no entity key, or an odd id). Then it first refreshes **without** zones,\nso the library removes them all, and then with the drawn zones."},"1984":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-36","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#refresh-rules","content":"The library's refresh compares against its own record of capability options. Removing a capability through\nthe SDK does not update that record, so the library would think it still exists. Letting the library remove\nand add keeps both in sync."},"1985":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-37","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#upgrading-the-library","content":"Raise `homey-esphomedriver` in `.homeycompose/app.json` (`pythonPackages`) and `requirements-dev.txt`."},"1986":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-38","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#upgrading-the-library","content":"Run `esphome-homey sync` to refresh the library-owned files: `.homeycompose/drivers/templates/`, the pair and\nrepair views, `.homeycompose/flow/`, the generic capabilities and icons, and the library's locale keys."},"1987":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-39","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#upgrading-the-library","content":"Delete what this app does not use: `.homeycompose/discovery/esphome.json` and `assets/logo.svg`."},"1988":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-40","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#upgrading-the-library","content":"Compare `.homeycompose/drivers/templates/esphome-defaults.json` with the app's own copies:"},"1989":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-41","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#upgrading-the-library","content":"new settings → add them to `drivers/s1pro/driver.settings.compose.json` (the app's settings file replaces\nthe template's settings, so they are copied there);"},"1990":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-42","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#upgrading-the-library","content":"new capabilities → add them to the `capabilities` list in `drivers/s1pro/driver.compose.json` (which leaves\nout the battery capabilities, so publish validation does not ask for battery information)."},"1991":{"id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver-43","page_id":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/esphomedriver#upgrading-the-library","content":"Run all checks and test on a real sensor."},"1992":{"id":"/docs/developers","page_id":"/docs/developers","type":"page","content":"Developers","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Developers"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/developers"},"1993":{"id":"/docs/developers-0","page_id":"/docs/developers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers","content":"How the app is built, and how to work on it."},"1994":{"id":"/docs/developers-1","page_id":"/docs/developers","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/developers#at-a-glance","content":"At a glance"},"1995":{"id":"/docs/developers-2","page_id":"/docs/developers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers","content":"The app is open source under the MIT licence:\ngithub.com/starredev/homey-sensy-s1pro. Bug reports, tested\nsensor setups and pull requests are welcome."},"1996":{"id":"/docs/developers-3","page_id":"/docs/developers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers","content":"Page"},"1997":{"id":"/docs/developers-4","page_id":"/docs/developers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers","content":"Contents"},"1998":{"id":"/docs/developers-5","page_id":"/docs/developers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers","content":"Architecture"},"1999":{"id":"/docs/developers-6","page_id":"/docs/developers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers","content":"Layers, the main classes and how data flows"},"2000":{"id":"/docs/developers-7","page_id":"/docs/developers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers","content":"homey-esphomedriver"},"2001":{"id":"/docs/developers-8","page_id":"/docs/developers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers","content":"What the shared ESPHome library does and how this app builds on it"},"2002":{"id":"/docs/developers-9","page_id":"/docs/developers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers","content":"Development setup"},"2003":{"id":"/docs/developers-10","page_id":"/docs/developers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers","content":"Tools, running the app on your Homey, Windows notes"},"2004":{"id":"/docs/developers-11","page_id":"/docs/developers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers","content":"Testing and CI"},"2005":{"id":"/docs/developers-12","page_id":"/docs/developers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers","content":"Test suites, coverage, linting, type checking and the CI workflows"},"2006":{"id":"/docs/developers-13","page_id":"/docs/developers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers","content":"Releasing"},"2007":{"id":"/docs/developers-14","page_id":"/docs/developers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers","content":"Versions, changelog, publishing to the Homey App Store, library upgrades"},"2008":{"id":"/docs/developers-15","page_id":"/docs/developers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers","content":"Documentation site"},"2009":{"id":"/docs/developers-16","page_id":"/docs/developers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers","content":"Working on this site"},"2010":{"id":"/docs/developers-17","page_id":"/docs/developers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers#at-a-glance","content":"**Homey Python app** (Python 3.14, Homey SDK v3, Homey 13+), id `io.github.starredev.sensy`."},"2011":{"id":"/docs/developers-18","page_id":"/docs/developers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers#at-a-glance","content":"Built on `homey-esphomedriver` and\n`aioesphomeapi`."},"2012":{"id":"/docs/developers-19","page_id":"/docs/developers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers#at-a-glance","content":"The **web views** (radar widget, zone editor) are plain JavaScript ES modules with their own Node tooling."},"2013":{"id":"/docs/developers-20","page_id":"/docs/developers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers#at-a-glance","content":"Quality gates: ruff, pyright (strict for `lib/`), pytest with ≥ 85 % coverage, ESLint and node:test for the\nweb views, and `homey app validate --level publish`."},"2014":{"id":"/docs/developers-21","page_id":"/docs/developers","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers#at-a-glance","content":"The previous Node.js implementation is kept on the\n`node` branch (tag `node-1.0.0`)."},"2015":{"id":"/docs/developers/releasing","page_id":"/docs/developers/releasing","type":"page","content":"Releasing","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Developers"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/developers/releasing"},"2016":{"id":"/docs/developers/releasing-0","page_id":"/docs/developers/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/releasing","content":"Versions, changelog and publishing to the Homey App Store."},"2017":{"id":"/docs/developers/releasing-1","page_id":"/docs/developers/releasing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/developers/releasing#versions-and-changelog","content":"Versions and changelog"},"2018":{"id":"/docs/developers/releasing-2","page_id":"/docs/developers/releasing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/developers/releasing#publishing-to-the-homey-app-store","content":"Publishing to the Homey App Store"},"2019":{"id":"/docs/developers/releasing-3","page_id":"/docs/developers/releasing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/developers/releasing#store-texts-and-images","content":"Store texts and images"},"2020":{"id":"/docs/developers/releasing-4","page_id":"/docs/developers/releasing","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/developers/releasing#app-id","content":"App id"},"2021":{"id":"/docs/developers/releasing-5","page_id":"/docs/developers/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/releasing#versions-and-changelog","content":"The app uses semantic versioning. For every release:"},"2022":{"id":"/docs/developers/releasing-6","page_id":"/docs/developers/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/releasing#versions-and-changelog","content":"Update `CHANGELOG.md` (move *Unreleased* to the new version)."},"2023":{"id":"/docs/developers/releasing-7","page_id":"/docs/developers/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/releasing#versions-and-changelog","content":"Add the user-facing changelog for the App Store to `.homeychangelog.json`, in English and Dutch."},"2024":{"id":"/docs/developers/releasing-8","page_id":"/docs/developers/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/releasing#versions-and-changelog","content":"Bump the version: `homey app version patch` (or `minor`, `major`). This updates `.homeycompose/app.json` and\n`app.json`."},"2025":{"id":"/docs/developers/releasing-9","page_id":"/docs/developers/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/releasing#versions-and-changelog","content":"Commit and push; wait for CI to pass."},"2026":{"id":"/docs/developers/releasing-10","page_id":"/docs/developers/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/releasing#publishing-to-the-homey-app-store","content":"`HOMEY_HEADLESS=1` skips the interactive questions: the version is not bumped and the changelog comes from\n`.homeychangelog.json` (publishing fails if the current version has no entry). Without it, the CLI asks whether\nto bump the version and whether you have read the\nApp Store guidelines."},"2027":{"id":"/docs/developers/releasing-11","page_id":"/docs/developers/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/releasing#publishing-to-the-homey-app-store","content":"The CLI validates the app at the *publish* level, compiles the Python dependencies for arm64 and amd64, uploads\nthe build and prints a link to the Developer Tools. There:"},"2028":{"id":"/docs/developers/releasing-12","page_id":"/docs/developers/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/releasing#publishing-to-the-homey-app-store","content":"Open the build."},"2029":{"id":"/docs/developers/releasing-13","page_id":"/docs/developers/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developers/releasing#publishing-to-the-homey-app-store","content":"**Release to Test** makes it installable through the app's test link."},"2030":{"id":"/docs/developers/releasing-14","page_id":"/docs/developers/releasing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/developer